    <div class="faq-c">&#128181; Collecting Payments</div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">How do I collect a payment from an existing customer?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Go to <strong>Collect Payment</strong> tab → search customer name → select them → enter amount → tap Collect. The amount is deducted from your wallet and posted to CRM.</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">What if the customer is not found in search?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">The customer may not be in CRM yet. Register them first via <strong>New KYC</strong>. After CRM sync completes, you can collect payments. You can also type the name manually.</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">Does the payment go to the CRM automatically?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Yes — when you collect a payment, it is posted to UCRM immediately via the API. UCRM then sends the customer an email receipt automatically. Your wallet is debited and the invoice is marked paid in UCRM in one step.</div></div>
