    <div class="faq-c">&#128178; Pricing &amp; Amounts</div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">How is the wallet deduction calculated for a Cash KYC registration?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">For <strong>Starlink</strong>: plan monthly price + hardware/kit price. For <strong>Fiber (FTTH)</strong>: plan monthly price + installation fee (configurable in Settings, default $100). For <strong>SIM</strong>: plan price only. The deduction equals the total amount the customer paid you.</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">I registered a cash customer — does the payment appear in CRM immediately?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Yes. When sales type is <strong>Cash</strong>, the plugin posts the payment immediately to UCRM as a credit balance on the customer account. The invoice is created later (after installation). UCRM automatically applies the credit when the invoice is generated — so the customer starts with zero balance.</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">What is a Credit registration vs Cash registration?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a"><strong>Cash</strong> — Customer paid the agent immediately. Wallet is debited, payment posted to CRM, customer created as Regular Client. <strong>Credit</strong> — Customer will pay later. No wallet deduction, no payment posted. Customer is created as a Lead in CRM until admin confirms payment received.</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">Where does the commission come from?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Commission is auto-calculated as a percentage of each collection (configurable per service type in Settings). For DishNet payroll staff commission is set to 0%. For external partner agents, the admin sets the rate. Commission is credited to the wallet automatically after each approved collection.</div></div>

    <div class="faq-c">&#128241; WhatsApp Notifications</div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">Why are WhatsApp notifications not sending?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Go to the <strong>💬 WhatsApp tab</strong> in the left sidebar (admin only). Enter: <strong>WASender Server URL</strong> (http://wa.dishnetafrica.com), <strong>App Key</strong>, and <strong>Auth Key</strong> — these are from the WASender server. Enter the phone numbers for Support and Accounts. Click <strong>Save WhatsApp Settings</strong>.</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">Which WhatsApp events are handled by WASender automatically (not by this plugin)?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">UCRM billing events are handled <strong>directly by WASender's built-in UCRM listener</strong> — our plugin never touches these: Invoice created, Payment received, Service suspended/restored, Client welcome. Our plugin only sends operational events that UCRM does not know about: KYC submitted, Wallet top-up, Recharge approved/rejected, Cash handover, Lead assigned, LTE alerts, Overdue reminders.</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">How do I send a manual WhatsApp notification?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Go to the <strong>Notify tab</strong> (admin only). Select event type, enter phone number and message → Send. You can also trigger installation confirmations, outage alerts, and commission summaries from there.</div></div>

    <div class="faq-c">&#128273; Usernames &amp; CRM IDs</div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">How are FTTH and Starlink usernames generated?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Usernames are auto-generated with a prefix + 6-digit number: <strong>Starlink → STAR000053</strong>, <strong>Fiber → FTTH000241</strong>. The number auto-increments from the last used number in the database. The admin can configure the starting number in <strong>Settings → Username Sequence</strong> to continue from the old system (e.g. set 52 for Starlink to get STAR000053 next).</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">Can an agent choose a custom CRM username?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Yes — on the KYC form there is an optional <strong>CRM Username</strong> field. If left blank, the system auto-generates FTTH/STAR username. If filled, the custom username is validated for uniqueness and format (letters, numbers, hyphens, underscores, 3–50 chars).</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">Can a username be changed after submission?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Admin can change the CRM username before the customer is provisioned (service activated). Go to <strong>All Applications</strong> → find the application → Edit Username. After provisioning, username changes must be done directly in UCRM.</div></div>

    <div class="faq-c">&#128202; Admin &amp; Accounts</div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">What does "Net Due to DishNet" mean in the ledger?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">It is the total amount the agent has collected from customers <strong>minus their earned commission</strong>. This is the amount the agent must remit to the company. Formula: <code>Net Due = Total Collected − Commission Earned</code>.</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">How does wallet recharge work for an agent?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Agent submits recharge request with payment proof (bank transfer / mobile money). Admin reviews and approves in <strong>Accounts → Recharge History</strong>. On approval, wallet is credited automatically. Rejected requests show the reason.</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">Why does an agent see "UCRM User ID Not Linked" on My Jobs?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">The agent's retailer profile needs a UCRM User ID to fetch their jobs. Admin: go to <strong>Retailers → Edit Retailer</strong> → find the <strong>UCRM User ID</strong> field → enter the number from UCRM's URL when viewing that user (e.g. /system/users/<strong>23</strong>/edit → enter 23).</div></div>
    <div class="faq-i"><div class="faq-q" onclick="this.parentElement.classList.toggle('op')">How do I approve or reject a wallet recharge request?<span class="ar">&#9660;</span></div><div class="faq-a">Go to <strong>Accounts → Recharge History</strong>. Pending requests show an Approve / Reject button. Approving immediately credits the agent's wallet and sends a WhatsApp confirmation. Rejecting requires a reason which is shown to the agent.</div></div>

